# Third-party data shipped with this project

verne80 is MIT (see LICENSE) and the page it produces is published under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
Two of the geometry layers it draws come from elsewhere, and one of them is copyleft.

## web/data/borders_1880.json — GPL-3.0

Derived from `geojson/world_1880.geojson` in **historical-basemaps** by **André Ourednik**
(https://github.com/aourednik/historical-basemaps), pinned to commit
`62d8f1a03a71f2d3ff17f2d166f7553f256bce68`.

That repository carries a plain, unmodified GNU General Public License v3.0 and no
separate licence for the data. The file committed here is a modified version of that
work: coordinates rounded to one decimal place, rings re-wound where the source wound a
hole as an exterior, features the source did not name removed, and everything dissolved
into a single geometry. **It is distributed under the GPL-3.0, not under this
repository's MIT licence.**

Whether the copyleft in fact reaches a rounded, re-wound extract of geometry is a
question of law rather than of fact, and it has not been resolved here — only recorded.
Anyone redistributing this file should reach their own view.

The source's own README says of the whole collection:

> It is __work in progress__: verify the maps by comparison to other sources before
> using in academic work.

## web/data/land.json and web/data/borders_modern.json — public domain

Derived from **Natural Earth** (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/), release `v5.1.2`,
files `ne_110m_land.geojson` and `ne_110m_admin_0_countries.geojson`. Natural Earth is
public domain: *"No permission is needed to use Natural Earth. Crediting the authors is
unnecessary."* The credit is given anyway.

## web/fonts — SIL Open Font License 1.1

